Subject: venus: the calling thread's id on macOS

macOS's SYS_gettid is not Linux's: it asks for a per-thread credential override and fails (-1), so every thread had the
same id, and two threads waiting on the ring both took themselves for the watchdog's owner: one unlocked the mutex the
other held. Strict sandboxes deny (and log) it besides, at every wait. The thread's Mach port needs no system call.

--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.h
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.h
@@ -646,6 +646,8 @@
    return gettid();
 #elif DETECT_OS_FREEBSD
    return syscall(SYS_thr_self);
+#elif DETECT_OS_APPLE /* SYS_gettid is something else there, and fails */
+   return pthread_mach_thread_np(pthread_self());
 #elif DETECT_OS_WINDOWS
    return GetCurrentThreadId();
 #else
